import lib/process.dl

function {process wait result:status} has no completion report:
    replacement:
        the inverse of (status reports completion)

function the nonblocking process test interpreter:
    execute:
        return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set command to a process command for the nonblocking process test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import os\nchunk=b'X'*4096\nwhile True:\n os.write(1,chunk)\n os.write(2,chunk)" as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it

read the standard output of child and set output to it
read the standard error of child and set error to it
poll child and set status to it
clean up child and set cleanup to it

print whether child was launched as a line
print whether output succeeded as a line
print whether (output's contents's length > 0) as a line
print whether error succeeded as a line
print whether (error's contents's length > 0) as a line
print whether status succeeded as a line
print whether status has no completion report as a line
print whether cleanup succeeded as a line
